WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.489
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.489 --> 00:00:07.680
In Captain America: Civil War, we learn that
with great power comes a great deal of government

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.680
supervision.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.290
Team Iron Man's ok with that; Team Cap, not
so much.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:16.030
And so the scene is set for the third of this
year's ideological bust-ups between comic

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.030
book characters.

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.269
First we had Daredevil versus the Punisher
in Season 2 of Marvel's Netflix show, and

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:23.689
then we had Batman v Superman.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:27.310
But now it's time for two of the lynchpins
of the Marvel Cinematic Universe to face off

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.480
in Captain America: Civil War.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.470
And it's been well worth the wait.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.590
Captain America: Civil War certainly has a
lot of plates to keep spinning, between being

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:40.410
the third instalment in a Captain America
trilogy, a sort of sequel to Age of Ultron,

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:44.620
an introduction to several new superheroes,
and an Avengers movie in everything other

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.620
than name.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.890
But don't worry as directors Anthony and Joe
Russo and screenwriters Christopher Markus

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:54.390
and Stephen McFeely deftly keep those plates
in pretty magnificent motion throughout.

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:58.160
The chemistry between the movie's many actors
and the connection you feel to their characters

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.490
has been slowly and steadily cooking for a
number of years now, and Civil War makes the

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:04.110
very most of that.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:08.420
At the heart of the movie are powerful, pitch-perfect
performances from Chris Evans and Robert Downey

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:09.490
Jr.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.680
Each actor is so obviously at ease in their
roles and has developed their respective characters

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.090
of Steve Rogers and Tony Stark so well over
the course of numerous films that it's a real

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.840
pleasure to watch them on screen as they battle
not only each other but their own inner conflicts.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.570
And it's fantastic seeing the welcome return
of so many other familiar faces too.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:31.270
Scarlett Johansson's Black Widow, Anthony
Mackie's Falcon, Don Cheadle's War Machine,

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:35.420
and Jeremy Renner's Hawkeye all get their
moments in and out of battle, though inevitably

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.450
some get more time to enjoy the spotlight
than others.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:42.910
Sebastian Stan is superb as Bucky Barnes aka
The Winter Soldier and his rapport with on-screen

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.610
best friend Chris Evans feels wonderfully
real.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:50.079
As the mysterious Zemo, Daniel Brühl gives
a nicely grounded, understated performance.

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:55.090
Paul Bettany continues the fine work as Vision
he started in Age of Ultron, and he and Elizabeth

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.060
Olsen get some delightful scenes together,
which both actors cleverly underplay as they

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:01.090
build their characters in intriguing ways.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:06.290
Paul Rudd's arrival as Ant-Man is a real joy
and he contributes some great moments to the

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:07.290
movie.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.260
I also really like Emily VanCamp as Sharon
Carter, aka Agent 13, and though her role

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.220
is a smaller supporting one compared to the
movie's many superheroes, she does get more

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:16.410
to do in this movie.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:20.810
However, one particular moment between Carter
and another character feels lacking in credible

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:21.810
build-up.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.620
And, as Everett K. Ross, Martin Freeman feels
a little wasted.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:29.930
Right from the very start, the action is full-on,
with plenty of wonderfully choreographed and

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:34.209
shot scenes that show the influence of movies
including The Raid and Bourne franchises and

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:37.930
demand your attention at every twist and turn
of the camera.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.720
And there's one particular action sequence
that's utterly spectacular, and is right up

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.350
there with the very best superhero action
scenes ever.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.280
The movie contains a wealth of humour too
which comes from a variety of sources including

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.000
Tony Stark, though he's necessarily more subdued
than usual.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.470
Falcon, Vision, Ant-Man, and new superhero
kid on the block, Spider-Man, also add a hell

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:00.620
of a lot in the comedy department.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.390
Speaking of Spider-Man and Peter Parker, his
scenes are an absolute treat!

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:09.879
As the latest actor to sport the Spidey spandex,
Tom Holland is simply outstanding, really

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:12.640
embodying the youthful spirit of the character.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:16.390
Spider-Man has always been one of my favourite
comic book characters, and I cannot wait to

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:20.420
see Holland continue the great groundwork
he's laid for the character here in his own

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.420
film.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.909
As for, Black Panther, our other new super-arrival,
actor Chadwick Boseman makes a great first

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:30.040
impression in the role, playing some really
interesting character-driven moments as well

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.370
as standing out in plenty of acrobatic action-filled
scenes.

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:38.390
Based on this movie, I'm certainly looking
forward to his first solo outing in 2018.

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:43.989
Oh, and Stan Lee gets the most fabulous cameo,
which is now one of my favourites.

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:48.220
One thing the movie doesn't always get quite
right is the level of consequences for some

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.220
of its plot points.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.569
But I can't say more without spoiling it.

00:03:51.569 --> 00:03:56.150
By the way, if you like Easter Eggs, then
Civil War's got stacks to keep a look-out

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.150
for.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.579
I've got a video about that on the way, and
I'll make the link live here as soon as it's

00:04:00.579 --> 00:04:01.579
ready.

00:04:01.579 --> 00:04:05.110
So, to sum up: Captain America: Civil War
is a compelling piece of cinema and one of

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.989
the MCU's best movies so far, which for me
means it's up there with the first Iron Man

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:14.810
movie, the first Avengers outing, The Winter
Soldier, and Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.201
Its action scenes are a breathless pleasure,
its humour is on point, its cast is a delight

00:04:19.201 --> 00:04:22.930
to watch, and its wealth of Easter Eggs is
enough to send you to nerdvana.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.480
It's a movie that deserves repeated viewings.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:27.880
And I'm already looking forward to watching
it again.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.080
Captain America: Civil War gets 4 and a half
out of 5 Flicks.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.790
Now, I'd love to know what you're looking
forward to about Captain America: Civil War,

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:36.810
and if you've already seen it, what did you
think?

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.730
Let me know in the comments below!

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:42.440
I've got lots more Captain America: Civil
War videos on the way including an Easter

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:45.190
Egg video and more spoilery discussion of
the movie.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:49.780
They'll all be in my Civil War playlist here
along with tons of cast interviews.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.720
If you enjoyed this video, I really appreciate
your liking and sharing it and subscribing!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.090
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:56.940
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

